WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.004 --> 00:00:06.994
A clean is never one-off. After a batch loads, the next run shows which records failed again.

2
00:00:06.994 --> 00:00:13.348
Per system: the score before and after the batch, records failing again and records fixed since.

3
00:00:13.348 --> 00:00:19.351
Rules failing again names the checks behind the records that came back on each system.

4
00:00:19.351 --> 00:00:26.654
The weekly trend, the drift by rule and the still-clean-by-batch tables sit under one fold. Open it.

5
00:00:26.654 --> 00:00:33.641
Failing again by week, against the records fixed. A rising line means the source keeps creating bad data.

6
00:00:33.641 --> 00:00:41.302
Drift by rule names the rules that come back, so the fix goes upstream to the process, not the record.

7
00:00:41.302 --> 00:00:48.621
Before and change show how far each rule has moved since the batch, so a growing gap stands out.

8
00:00:48.621 --> 00:00:53.624
Still clean by batch: each loaded batch with the records that stayed fixed.
